# NOTE: .gitignore does NOT support trailing comments on a pattern line.
# `docs/mockups/   # 229 MB` is a literal pattern including the spaces and the
# hash, and matches nothing. Comments live on their own lines only.

# ── dependencies + build output ──────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
.next/
out/
dist/
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# ── secrets ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.local
.env*.local
!.env.example

# ── local dev artefacts ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# app/.smoke-app is a throwaway copy of the app that e2e/bookings-smoke.mjs
# runs its own dev server from — Next refuses two dev servers on one directory,
# and the copy has no .env.local, which is what guarantees the test can never
# reach the real Resend key. The script deletes it; this is for when it does not.
# The wildcard also covers any .smoke-*.png / .smoke-*.mjs left behind by a run.
.smoke-*

# ── AND EVERY OTHER THROWAWAY COPY OF THE APP ────────────────────────────────
# `.smoke-*` above covered the suites' copies and nothing else, so
# `app/.shots-media-app` — a screenshot probe's copy of the whole app, made by
# e2e/_tmp-media-shots.mjs — was committed and pushed: 370 files of a stale
# duplicate `src/`. It cost real confusion. The Replit agent reading the
# repository concluded the new application "is stored in an
# app/.shots-media-app/ snapshot rather than the deployed app/ root" and built
# a merge plan around it.
#
# So: any dot-directory that ends in `-app`, and the scratch prefixes the
# probes use. A copy of the application is never a thing to commit.
.*-app/
.rehearsal/
_tmp-*
_probe*
_shot-*
_d[0-9]*-tmp*
.storage/
*.log
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.tmp-rings/
pipeline/
contexts/

# ── design-stage artefacts: REGENERABLE and large ────────────────────────────
# The factory's working output, not the product. 229 MB of rejected direction
# variants, 125 MB of review screenshots, 54 MB of craft renders. Regenerate
# from the factory if ever needed.
docs/mockups/
docs/visual-review/
docs/_screen-craft/
docs/_screen-craft-render.json
docs/_mockup-craft-render.json
docs/_dispatch/

# ── image MASTERS ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The generated brand images at source resolution — 106 MB, averaging 6.7 MB
# each. Too large for git and NOT what is served: the app serves the optimised
# derivatives in app/public/media/ (5.3 MB, 95% smaller — DECISIONS-BUILD D-6).
#
# KEEP THE MASTERS SAFE ELSEWHERE. They are the only source for re-deriving at
# another size, and they cannot be regenerated identically — they came from a
# generative model. Object storage or a backup drive, not here.
assets/images/

# ── factory tooling that is not part of the product ──────────────────────────
.claude/
schemas/
plans/
scripts/
justfile
mcp-defaults-design.json
brief-template.md
brief.manifest.json

# the brand marks ARE committed — small vectors, load-bearing
!assets/brand/
!assets/brand/**

# session scratch/debug artefacts
docs/_craft-tmp/
docs/_*.png
docs/_tmp*
.tmp-scratch/
_tmp_*
docs/_results/
docs/_flow-interactions-*.json
docs/screens/_results/
docs/_integration-decision-brief.md

# factory scaffolding that is not part of the product and misleads tooling
pnpm-workspace.yaml
turbo.json

# agentflow factory tooling — not part of the product
CLAUDE.md
AGENTS.md
app/CLAUDE.md
app/AGENTS.md
companion/

# Runtime state. Holds the admin password hash — never commit it.
app/data/

# ── Replit-side build artefacts ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# Generated inside the Replit workspace, not part of the source. Ignored so a
# Replit -> GitHub sync never drags them in. NOTE: .replit itself IS tracked on
# purpose — it carries the deployment build command, including the
# --include=dev that stops NODE_ENV=production deleting the build toolchain.
artifacts/

# ── scratch from agent verification runs ─────────────────────────────────────
# Throwaway probes, built-module copies and screenshots. They are useful while
# a change is being proved and worthless afterwards; they were nearly committed
# once, which is why they are named here rather than remembered.
app/_tmp-*/
app/diag-tmp.mjs
app/e2e/_*
app/.smoke-*
app/shot-*.png
docs/screens/**/_verify*.mjs
docs/screens/**/_splice-tmp.mjs
docs/screens/**/_states/_verify-*.png

# Superseded by the built page at docs/screens/webapp/workshop-detail.html.
docs/screens/webapp/workshop-detail-reading-the-field.html

# ── camera masters ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# C0260.MP4 is 604 MB of raw 4K straight off the camera. The web derivative
# beside it (2.3 MB, 1280×720, faststart) is the one the pages reference, and
# is small enough to keep. Masters stay on disk and out of the history.
assets/videos/*.MP4
assets/videos/*.mp4
!assets/videos/the-room-web.mp4
assets/videos/_contact.jpg
docs/screens/**/_patch*-tmp.mjs
docs/screens/workshopflow/_frag/_tmp-gallery.part
docs/screens/workshopflow/_gen-awb.mjs
# Dropped 2026-08-12: admin-offerings' Workshops tab subsumed it.
docs/screens/workshopflow/admin-workshops-list.html
docs/screens/workshopflow/_frag/admin-workshops-list.html

# Agent scratch at the app root (probe-tmp, check-tmp and friends).
app/*-tmp.mjs
app/_tmp-*

# Splice scratch under the screens directories.
docs/screens/**/_tmp-*

# The app's OWN build scripts are part of the product and are committed.
#
# `scripts/` above was written for the factory's tooling at the repository root,
# but a bare directory name in .gitignore matches at every depth — so it was
# also swallowing app/scripts/, which is where build-email-logo.mjs lives. That
# script generates app/public/brand/logo-horizontal@2x.png from the SVG, and a
# committed asset whose generator is untracked is an asset nobody can re-derive.
!app/scripts/
!app/scripts/**

# Agent test uploads — brown rectangles from a smoke run, not media.
app/public/media/tmp-*
docs/_d23-tmp.md
